---
// The agent kit: what its four blocks are, and the kit in every theme.
import Layout from "@/layouts/Base.astro"
import SectionHeader from "@/components/SectionHeader.astro"
import { REPO_URL } from "@/lib/brand"
import { kitBlocks, kitUrls, SITE_THEME, themes } from "@/lib/themes"

const first = themes.find((theme) => theme.slug === SITE_THEME) ?? themes[0]
const words = ["Zero", "One", "Two", "Three", "Four", "Five", "Six", "Seven", "Eight"]
const count = words[kitBlocks.length] ?? String(kitBlocks.length)
---

<Layout
  title="Agent kit: blocks for agent interfaces | Strict"
  description="Free React blocks for an agent's side of a conversation: a tool call, an approval, a streaming answer and its sources. Written out for each Strict theme, and checked against it."
>
  <section class="border-b border-border">
    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-page gap-8 px-4 py-16 md:grid-cols-12 md:px-8">
      <p class="label text-muted-foreground md:col-span-12">Agent kit</p>
      <h1 class="text-h1 md:col-span-9 md:text-display">Blocks for the agent's side of the conversation.</h1>
      <p class="md:col-span-6">
        {count} React blocks for an interface where an agent works: what it called, what it
        asks leave for, what it is writing, and what it read. Each is one file you own, built
        on Base UI and Tailwind, and written out for the theme you pick, in that theme's
        spacing, type and colors.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="mx-auto flex max-w-page flex-col gap-16 px-4 py-16 md:px-8">
    <section class="flex flex-col gap-8">
      <SectionHeader number="01" label="The blocks" title="One file each. No library to install." id="blocks" />
      <ul class="grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-2">
        {
          kitBlocks.map((block) => (
            <li class="flex flex-col gap-2 border-t border-border pt-4">
              <h3 class="font-heading text-h2">{block.title}</h3>
              <p class="text-muted-foreground">{block.description}</p>
              <p class="label text-muted-foreground">components/agent/{block.file}</p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
      <p class="max-w-measure text-muted-foreground">
        They hold no state of their own beyond open and closed: your code says whether a
        call is running, whether a request was allowed, and what the answer is so far. The
        source is in{" "}
        <a href={`${REPO_URL}/tree/master/packages/kit`} class="text-link underline underline-offset-4"
          >packages/kit</a
        >.
      </p>
    </section>

    {
      first && (
        <section class="flex flex-col gap-8">
          <SectionHeader number="02" label="Look" title={`The kit in ${first.name}.`} id="look" />
          <div class="rounded-md border border-border bg-card p-2 md:p-4">
            <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-sm border border-border" data-strict-ignore>
              <iframe
                src={kitUrls(first.slug).build}
                title={`The agent kit, built with ${first.name}`}
                class="block w-full bg-background"
                style="height:80svh"></iframe>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      )
    }

    <section class="flex flex-col gap-8">
      <SectionHeader number="03" label="Themes" title="Pick the theme. The kit follows it." id="themes" />
      <p class="max-w-measure text-muted-foreground">
        A block does not carry sizes of its own. For each theme it is written out again:
        a gap is that theme's spacing step, a label is that theme's label size in its label
        font. Every one of them is run through Strict Check in light and dark mode, at two
        widths, with hover and focus.
      </p>
      <ul class="grid gap-x-8 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
        {
          themes.map((theme) => (
            <li class="border-t border-border py-4">
              <a
                href={kitUrls(theme.slug).page}
                class="font-heading text-h2 underline-offset-4 hover:underline"
              >
                {theme.name}
              </a>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
